# INF-DP-11 -- logrotate rules for xbrain process logs
#
# Installed to /etc/logrotate.d/xbrain by the deploy script. Rotates
# each process's log file separately so a single hot process (e.g.
# p1_motion at 20 Hz) does not trip rotation on quiet processes.
#
# Why weekly, not daily. Daily rotation on a 20 Hz process produces
# small files and heavy fs churn; weekly + size caps hit the same
# ceiling with fewer files.
#
# missingok is intentional: a service that never started (Stage 0
# blocked it) never writes a log file, and that must not fail rotate.
#
# copytruncate is intentional: the processes keep the file open via a
# python logging FileHandler; without copytruncate, rotate would move
# the file and the process would keep writing to the now-hidden inode.

/opt/xbrain_v6/data/logs/*.log {
    weekly
    rotate 8
    size 100M
    missingok
    notifempty
    compress
    delaycompress
    copytruncate
    dateext
    dateformat -%Y%m%d
}
